📅 Day 41 – ES6 Features (Arrow Functions & Promises)

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on modern JavaScript (ES6 features), specifically arrow functions and promises, which improve code readability and handle asynchronous operations efficiently.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Arrow Functions
Short and concise way to write functions
Uses => syntax
No need for function keyword

🔹 Syntax:
const add = (a, b) => {
    return a + b;
};

Key Points:
Cleaner and shorter syntax
Implicit return for single expressions
Does not have its own this
2️⃣ Promises
Used to handle asynchronous operations
Helps avoid callback hell
Represents a future value
Promise States:
Pending → Initial state
Resolved (Fulfilled) → Operation successful
Rejected → Operation failed
3️⃣ Handling Promises
.then() → Handles success
.catch() → Handles errors
🔹 Practical Work
Created arrow functions for different tasks
Implemented promise-based examples
Observed asynchronous execution flow
Tested success and error handling